{
  "_comment": "Titans are DATA (CLAUDE.md §11). A run fights them in order (see Run.ENCOUNTERS). Move types: attack (hits the telegraphed hunter), attack_all (sweeps BOTH — shakes each hunter DOWN to the ledge below, and rewards blocking/Cover), block (guards), enrage (permanently +value to its attacks this fight — a soft timer that rewards focus-fire). weak_point_height = the sigil Height; ledges = safe rest Heights on the way up (climb between them before your grip timer runs out, SotC-style). limiter = {type, value}: one generic rule this Titan bends against a specific strategy, applied by Combat._apply_limiter() at the start of its turn (design/sts2-comparison.md §3.4) — 'wound_decay' sheds `value` Wound/turn (punishes stack-and-wait Poison), 'sigil_fatigue' chips a hunter camped at the sigil more than `value` rounds running, 'height_split' chips a hunter more than `value` Height above their ally (punishes one hunter hoarding the climb). Tuned for two players; retune freely during balance. 'thorns' (backlog #36, static): a hunter who deals card damage to this Titan takes this much back (Combat._damage_boss). 'artifact' (backlog #36, static seed, spent as the fight goes — see Boss.apply_dict): wards this many of the hunters' Expose/Poison/Frail applications before they land (Combatant.try_block_debuff). 'pools' groups beasts by map node type: quick fights, elites, and the act-ending Titans. A move can also carry 'when' (backlog #40): {type: 'min_height'|'max_height'|'at_sigil'|'undefended', value: int}, checked against every hunter's foothold/Block at the moment the move comes up in the pattern (Boss.current_move(context), context built by Combat.boss_context()) — true if ANY hunter meets it. When 'when' is present the move also needs a sibling 'fallback' move (same {type, value} shape) used instead when the condition fails; a move with no 'when' always fires, unconditionally, exactly as before this field existed. 'hurt_pct' + 'hurt_moves' (backlog #44): once HP drops to or below `hurt_pct` of max_hp, Boss.current_move() reads `hurt_moves` instead of `moves` for the rest of the fight (same _move_index drives both, so the switch lands wherever the pattern already was, not a reset to move 1) — 'when'/'fallback' still work inside hurt_moves. Omit both (the default) for a beast with one pattern for the whole fight, unchanged from before this field existed. 'adds' (backlog #63): a list of secondary combatants clinging to this Titan — a parasite, a guardian on a hold — each {id, name, max_hp, moves}. Every add is a real (small) Boss built by Content.build_boss_adds(), NOT a separate top-level entry here, so it carries no art-coverage or beast-pool requirement of its own. Only 'attack' and 'block' move types are honoured for an add (Combat._adds_turn()) — it's a thin secondary threat, not a second full Titan. Card damage reaches an add only when a play explicitly names it (Combat.play_card()'s `enemy_index`) or the card carries `hits_all_enemies` (Cleave); every ordinary card keeps hitting the main boss exactly as before this field existed. Killing the boss still ends the fight regardless of any add left standing — adds are extra things to fight, not extra things you must kill to win. Omit (the default) for a beast with just the one body, unchanged from before this field existed. 'frail' (backlog #69) and 'curse' (backlog #69) are the first two move types that hit the HUNTER rather than dealing HP damage — until now every Titan only ever dealt damage, so the debuff axis (#36 Frail/Artifact/Thorns) and curses (#27) only ever came from cards and events, never from the thing they were supposedly fighting. 'frail' applies `value` stacks of Frail to the currently-targeted hunter through Combat._apply_frail() — the exact same generic function a card uses to Frail the Titan, so it is warded by that hunter's own Artifact stack first, same as any other debuff. 'curse' shoves `value` (default 1 if omitted/0) copies of a status card into the targeted hunter's DISCARD pile — a real card, not a stat, so Artifact does not ward it off (matching the precedent an event's own `curse_card`, backlog #27, already set: a curse is a thing you're handed, not a debuff applied to you). Names the card via an optional 'card' key (default 'bruised_grip', the only status card that exists today).",
